Rule 1 (non-empty shapes tuple to avoid AssertionError)
{v_1 : tuple(tuple(int))} |= v_1.len ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (each dimension in a shape must be non-negative to avoid negative-dimension error)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (binary broadcastability with right-aligned dimensions to avoid shape-mismatch)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, if v_1.len ≥ v_2.len then v_1.len - 1 else v_2.len - 1] : if i ≤ v_1.len - 1 then if i ≤ v_2.len - 1 then v_1[v_1.len - 1 - i] = 1 ∨ v_2[v_2.len - 1 - i] = 1 ∨ v_1[v_1.len - 1 - i] = v_2[v_2.len - 1 - i] else v_1[v_1.len - 1 - i] = 1 else if i ≤ v_2.len - 1 then v_2[v_2.len - 1 - i] = 1
>>
Rule 4 (three-shape broadcastability with aligned lengths to avoid shape-mismatch)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : tuple(int), v_3 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = v_2.len ∧ v_2.len = v_3.len ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] = 1 ∨ v_2[i] = 1 ∨ v_3[i] = 1 ∨ (v_1[i] = v_2[i] ∧ v_1[i] = v_3[i])
>>
Rule 5 (scalar-shape broadcast: an empty shape broadcasts with any non-negative shape)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 0 ∧ ∀j ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[j] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 6 (all dimensions non-negative for two shapes to avoid negative-dimension error)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : tuple(int)} |= (∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0) ∧ (∀j ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[j] ≥ 0)
